<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1620corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 16 to 20 corrections"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1620corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.0.0 (2026-11-26): Mission stage only (one stage per version). Opened on the owner's instruction of 2026-11-26 16:57 Istanbul ("Let's finish incoming chapters first as they are candidates for incoming lectures. After the completion we can return to the covered chapters in previous sessions"). READING OF THE INSTRUCTION, stated so it can be corrected: the incoming chapters are those after chapter 15 that have a deck, chapters 16 to 20; chapters 21 to 25 have a page but no deck and are not taken; chapters 1 to 9 are the covered chapters of earlier sessions the owner will return to.
ORDINAL AND ONE-AT-A-TIME CHECK: the live register files were read on 2026-11-26. Lineage12 (chapters 12 to 15) is LS_Archived (register 1.28.0, closure report in 07-lineage); Lineage11 and Lineage10 are archived; Lineages 4 to 9 are LS_Achieved. Lineage3 (chapters 9 and 10) still reads LS_InProgress in its own register (sen0414_ch09ch10_lineage_v1_7_0.ttl) as it did when Lineages 4 to 12 opened; it is a finding for the chapters 1 to 9 work and is not run or touched here. The highest ordinal in the register and its archives is 12; the next free ordinal is 13.
OE CEREMONY: the rules governing this stage were read from the highest OE governance ABox (oegov_abox_v1_56_0.ttl on GitHub) with rdflib: BP-D2 (read the bytes, not a summary), BP-D7 and BP-D62 (a changed file gets a new version, sized to the change), BP-D63 and B8 (plain talk with the owner), L-64 (stay in own scope), L-65 and L-66 (verify claims by re-reading and use only declared measurements), L-78 (act when rules and evidence decide), L-113 (every named item gets its own disposition), L-114 (append corrections, label a gap against a safeguard), L-118 (labels before identifiers). Enforcement: backlog_next_act check before every step, one commit per stage, git as the witness of order. The Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7 and the Lineage Practice Guide v1.0.0 were fetched from GitHub the same day.
VERIFIED GAPS (live files measured 2026-11-26 with the deck checks of deckchecks_runner.sh (deck standard 1.3.0, fit, layout, notes, overlap, reader notes, story prose), cme_material_check 1.0.2 on the newest deck and page of each chapter, a phrase scan of slide text and notes, a count of everyday-analogy marker slides, a count of code slides with two result balloons, the page-shapes check on the newest page A-box where one exists and a count of older page drafts; logs in 08-tooling/lineage13-opening/). Chapter 16 (deck 4.0.0, page 9.99.0): deck standard 13 of 13, fit, layout, notes, overlap, reader notes and story prose clean, material check 8 of 8, 0 analogy-marked slides, 25 of 25 code slides with two result balloons; page has no run-in-order menu item (0 occurrences) and its newest page A-box (9.95.0, older than the page) does not conform to the page shapes; 8 older page drafts. Chapter 17 (deck 4.0.0, page 9.23.0): the same clean deck and material results, 28 of 28 code slides with two result balloons; no run-in-order menu item; no page A-box file exists in the chapter folder, so the page shapes cannot be run; 6 older page drafts. Chapter 18 (deck 3.0.0, page 9.100.0): deck standard 13 of 13 and material check 8 of 8; reader-note check 94 findings; fit check refuses slide 43 (two frames overlap); 9 analogy-marked slides; 5 phrases of the think-of kind in slide text; 0 of 27 code slides with two result balloons; no run-in-order menu item; page A-box 9.95.0 does not conform; 9 older page drafts. Chapter 19 (deck 2.2.0, page 9.98.0): deck standard 13 of 13 and material check 8 of 8; 49 reader-note findings; fit check refuses slide 16; 8 analogy-marked slides; 1 phrase in slide text and 2 in notes; 0 of 18 code slides with two result balloons; no run-in-order menu item; no page A-box file; 7 older page drafts. Chapter 20 (deck 2.0.1, page 9.100.0): deck standard 13 of 13 and material check 8 of 8; 45 reader-note findings; 8 analogy-marked slides; 0 of 19 code slides with two result balloons; no run-in-order menu item; no page A-box file; 8 older page drafts. Every page is on template 9.28.0 and carries no lambda and no analogy words; no deck carries a prompt marker or the word lambda. Older page drafts in all five chapters: 38.
NOT MEASURED YET (named, not dropped): whether the five pages pass the full page test on the current pipeline; whether the chapter code, the page and the lab libraries carry matching code; whether story pictures and links of chapters 18 to 20 are current; the story-repeat check over chapters 16 to 20 against all others. They are measured in the scope stage before any goal rests on them.
WHY A NEW LINEAGE: Lineage12 is closed and archived, and a closed lineage is revived only in extraordinary cases; chapters 16 to 20 are a different closeable slice, chosen by the owner because they are the next lecture subjects.
REDUCING REWORK: chapters 16 and 17 were re-cut by Lineage10 and need only the run-in-order item and the removal of old drafts; chapters 18 to 20 are rebuilt once through the generic chapter builder from a spec and each page through the lambda-free A-box maker and the page test, the conversion pattern of Lineage12 is reused, not rebuilt."""@en,
        "1.1.0 (2026-11-26): Scope stage only (one stage per version): the scope statement with its areas, deliverables and exclusions, derived from the Mission stage's verified gaps (Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3d). The shape rules that the Lineage12 scope stage found only on a second pass are answered here at once (each area has a location, a counted measure and a layer; each deliverable a layer and a quoted mission clause; each exclusion a concern, a layer and a decision-maker). The four gaps named NOT MEASURED in 1.0.0 are scope items here (page test on the current pipeline, matching code, links and pictures, story repeat) and are measured before any goal rests on them. Lesson taken from the Lineage12 closure: an exclusion names the act it forbids exactly (modifying or deleting an existing file), so that the planned new own-version files do not read as a breach, and the folders allowed to change are listed in the scope text."@en,
        "1.10.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 2 (chapter 17) planned: refinement and planning events for ST13_Page_17 and ST13_Release_17, five typed tasks; ST13_Page_17 and its first task start."@en,
        "1.11.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 2, story ST13_Page_17 Done: chapter 17 page 9.100.0 built and tested (three tasks Done with evidence in 08-tooling/lineage13-opening/ch17_page_9_100_0/ and 08-tooling/ch17-page/logs_v9_100_0/)."@en,
        "1.12.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 2 (chapter 17) done: ST13_Release_17 Done, with the release record and the twelve verdicts; the stories of the package are Done."@en,
        "1.13.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 3 (chapter 18) planned: refinement and planning events for ST13_Spec_18, ST13_Deck_18, ST13_Page_18, ST13_Release_18 and ST13_Measure_Links, typed tasks; ST13_Spec_18 and its first task start."@en,
        "1.14.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 3, story ST13_Spec_18 Done: spec 4.0.0 of chapter 18 written and run through the generic builder 2.10.0; ST13_Deck_18 and its first task start."@en,
        "1.15.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 3, story ST13_Deck_18 Done: deck 4.0.0 of chapter 18 built and checked; ST13_Page_18 and its first task start."@en,
        "1.16.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 3, story ST13_Page_18 Done: chapter 18 page 9.101.0 built and tested; ST13_Release_18 and its first task start."@en,
        "1.17.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 3, story ST13_Measure_Links started: the link and picture check of chapters 18 to 20 is done (all 42 links answer 200, 3 drawn pictures recorded); two sentences of the chapter 18 notes corrected by new versions (deck 4.0.1, page 9.102.0), appended to the deck and page stories."@en,
        "1.18.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 3: deck 4.0.1 of chapter 18 built and checked (correction after the link check); the page 9.102.0 follows."@en,
        "1.19.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 3: page 9.102.0 of chapter 18 built and checked; Measure_Links Done."@en,
        "1.2.0 (2026-11-26): Goal stage only (one stage per version). Derived from Scope13, not from a list of gaps (Lineage Operating Discipline v163.0.7, 3d): one mission-facing goal; scope-facing goals that between them cover all nine areas; one containment-facing goal; one exclusion-facing goal for each of the five exclusions. Each goal states the benefit of what the work implements; the conditions of the record are measured by the objectives of the next stage."@en,
        "1.20.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 3 (chapter 18) done: ST13_Release_18 Done, with the release record and the twelve verdicts."@en,
        "1.21.0 (2026-11-26): Route recorded for the Owner's order of work after chapter 20 (queued lineages for chapters 21 to 25, then the earliest chapters); scope of this lineage unchanged."@en,
        "1.22.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 4 (chapter 19) planned: refinement and planning events for ST13_Spec_19, ST13_Deck_19, ST13_Page_19 and ST13_Release_19 with typed tasks."@en,
        "1.23.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 4, story ST13_Spec_19 Done: spec 4.0.0 of chapter 19 written and run by the generic builder 2.10.0."@en,
        "1.24.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 4, story ST13_Deck_19 Done: deck 4.0.0 of chapter 19 built and checked."@en,
        "1.25.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 4, story ST13_Page_19 Done: chapter 19 page 9.99.0 built and tested."@en,
        "1.26.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 4 (chapter 19) done: ST13_Release_19 Done, with the release record and the twelve verdicts."@en,
        "1.27.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5 (chapter 20 and the closing stories) planned: refinement and planning events for ST13_Spec_20, ST13_Deck_20, ST13_Page_20, ST13_Release_20, ST13_Measure_MatchingCode, ST13_Measure_PageTest, ST13_OwnVersions and ST13_Guards with typed tasks."@en,
        "1.28.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5, story ST13_Spec_20 Done: spec 4.0.0 of chapter 20 written and run by the generic builder 2.10.0."@en,
        "1.29.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5, story ST13_Deck_20 Done: deck 4.0.0 and manifest 1.2.0 of chapter 20 built, all deck checks clean."@en,
        "1.3.0 (2026-11-26): Objective stage only (one stage per version). Each goal is measured by objectives (26 in all), each metric derived from its goal, each with a counted, derived or judged measurement and a query that reads it, a baseline measured on 2026-11-26 (logs in 08-tooling/lineage13-opening/; the balloon, own-version, spec and page counts from the files named in each query) and a baseline observation. Objectives whose figure is met by absence carry the direction Hold: their figure is read at every observation and can rise. The balloon target is the real count of code slides (117 = 25 + 28 + 27 + 18 + 19); the rdodi objective counts existing files modified or deleted, so new files there are allowed by this objective only where the scope allows them; the allowed folders of the outside-files objective are listed in its query. The objectives are written by the table script 08-tooling/lineage13-opening/objective_make_v1_0_0.py, a lineage's own script, disclosed. Checkpoint dates are forecasts, never deadlines. The goals of 1.2.0 already carry their origin and decider."@en,
        "1.30.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5: deck 4.0.1 and manifest 1.2.1 of chapter 20 (sourced AT&T photograph instead of the drawing), checks clean."@en,
        "1.31.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5, story ST13_Page_20 Done: page 9.101.0 of chapter 20 built, A-box, page test and shapes passed."@en,
        "1.32.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5 (chapter 20) done: ST13_Release_20 Done, with the release record and the twelve verdicts."@en,
        "1.33.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5, story ST13_Measure_MatchingCode Done: manifests, pages and Lab cells of chapters 16 to 20 match in 117 of 117 examples; lab libraries recorded for the lab lineage."@en,
        "1.34.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5, story ST13_Measure_PageTest Done: 5 of 5 pages of chapters 16 to 20 pass the page test."@en,
        "1.35.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5, story ST13_OwnVersions Done: 44 older page drafts of chapters 16 to 20 removed, version check exit 0."@en,
        "1.36.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 5, story ST13_Guards Done: no guarded file and no file outside the allowed folders changed."@en,
        "1.37.0 (2026-11-26): Final observations of the 26 objectives, measured from the final files (final_measure_v1_0_0.py and its log, the final_*.log files of the checks, and the earlier closure logs, all in 08-tooling/lineage13-closure and 08-tooling/lineage13-opening). One objective, ContentChanged, is not at target by the letter and carries an appended correction note; the spec objective is above its target."@en,
        "1.38.0 (2026-11-26): Closure of Lineage13 by partial achievement. All stories and tasks Done; 26 objectives observed (1.37.0), 25 at target, ContentChanged not at target by the letter (5 changes no ruling forces, all recorded-paragraph wordings). Per the Owner's ruling of 2026-11-26 no confirmation is needed once the conditions hold; they hold. Outcome Out_Achieved with the partial reading stated in the closure report: 07-lineage/CLOSURE_REPORT_sen0414_ch1620corr_lineage_Lineage13_v1_0_0.md. The archive step goes in the next release."@en,
        "1.39.0 (2026-11-26): The register root no longer belongs to the lineage: it keeps only its label, identifier and isRegisterRoot, as the archival partition rule requires (the form of Lineage12 1.27.0); its definition of done and commitment stay on the backlog of Lineage13, and the commitment belongs to the lineage."@en,
        "1.4.0 (2026-11-26): Backlog stage of Lineage13: the register root, the backlog, 22 stories with acceptance criteria and links to the objectives they move and the deliverables they satisfy, and the lineage's own Definition of Done. Tasks follow in the planning stage, where each is produced by a planning event. CORRECTION OF 1.3.0 (appended, never edited): the spec objective of 1.3.0 said that none of the five chapters has a spec folder and set the target at 5. Both were wrong: specs exist (chapter 16 spec_v4_0_0, chapter 17 spec_v4_0_0, chapter 18 spec_v3_0_0, chapter 19 spec, chapter 20 spec_v2_0_1) and the newest decks were built from them by the generic builder versions 2.9.0, 2.6.0, 2.4.0, 2.2.0 and 2.3.0. The baseline 0 stays true read as chapters whose newest deck is built by the current generic builder 2.10.0; the target is 3, the chapters 18 to 20 that are re-cut, because chapters 16 and 17 need no re-cut (mission: reduce rework). The wrong text stays visible in 1.3.0."@en,
        "1.5.0 (2026-11-26): Planning stage of Lineage13: five packages (one per chapter, the last also carrying the closing stories), five time-boxed iterations that match them, and the planning of the first iteration only (refinement, planning events, typed tasks). Iterations 2 to 5 are planned when they start, by small steps. Dates are forecasts, never deadlines."@en,
        "1.6.0 (2026-11-26): Merged register. Deltas 1.0.0 to 1.5.0 combined into one file; hasState, hasLineageStatus, hasMissionOutcome, checkpointDate, hasForecastDate, hasForecastRationale, hasTargetValue, metricTarget and expectedValue take their latest value (the corrected spec target 3 of 1.4.0 stands; the earlier values stay in git history); every other statement is kept. Moves recorded here: the lineage is In progress, story ST13_Page_16 and its first task are InProgress (iteration 1 starts). Made by the lineage's own script register_step_v1_0_0.py."@en,
        "1.7.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 1, story ST13_Page_16 Done: chapter 16 page 9.100.0 built and tested (three tasks Done with evidence in 08-tooling/lineage13-opening/ch16_page_9_100_0/ and 08-tooling/ch16-page/logs_v9_100_0/)."@en,
        "1.8.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 1, story ST13_Measure_StoryRepeat Done: the story-repeat measurement of chapters 16 to 20 is recorded (one of the four unmeasured items)."@en,
        "1.9.0 (2026-11-26): Iteration 1 (chapter 16) done: ST13_Release_16 Done, with the release record and the twelve verdicts; the three stories of the package are Done."@en ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1620corr-lineage/1.39.0> , <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1620corr-lineage/1.38.0> ;
